SUMMARY:Data sonification
DESCRIPTION:This workshop introduces the core concepts behind mapping dat
 a to pitch\, tempo\, and timbre\, and demonstrates a few accessible tools
  for turning a dataset into an audio track. We'll work through a simple e
 xample together so participants can hear how sonification reveals structu
 re in time-series or other sequential data. GUI interfaces will be used s
 o no musical or coding background required—though we'll point to R and 
 Python libraries for those who want to go further.__________  New to rese
 arch\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more abo
 ut research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester
 \, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of resear
 ching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting
  funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries
 \, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessio
 ns useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advance
 d registration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Rese
 arch Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and do
 n't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">This workshop 
 introduces the core concepts behind mapping data to pitch\, tempo\, and t
 imbre\, and demonstrates a few accessible tools for turning a dataset int
 o an audio track. We'll work through a simple example together so partici
 pants can hear how sonification reveals structure in time-series or other
  sequential data. GUI interfaces will be used so no musical or coding bac
 kground required—though we'll point to R and Python libraries for those
  who want to go further.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&qu
 ot\;:false\,&quot\;134233118&quot\;:false\,&quot\;335559738&quot\;:240\,&
 quot\;335559739&quot\;:0}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="none">_____
 _____</span></p><p>  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or
  interested in learning more about research data support at IU? Over the 
 course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk 
 you through the basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing 
 and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding the righ
 t tools.</p><p>  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, 
 and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any s
 tage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.</p><p>  For any qu
 estions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (<a
  href="mailto:resdata@iu.edu">resdata@iu.edu</a>) - and don't forget to c
 heck back regularly\, as new sessions are added!</p>
