BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries
DTSTART:20261102T170000Z
DTEND:20261102T180000Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
SUMMARY:Lilly Library Photography Collection Visit
DESCRIPTION:Join the Lilly Library's Curator of Photography for this behi
 nd-the-scenes look at photographs from their permanent collection. As Ind
 iana University's main library for rare books\, manuscripts\, and special
  collections participants will learn the role that photography plays thro
 ughout the Lilly Library's collections. In addition to viewing a wonderfu
 l selection from throughout photographic history\, we will get to hear ab
 out the upcoming exhibition Harnessing Light: Tracing Time Through Photog
 raphy opening at the Lilly Library early next year.Scott McMahon is Curat
 or of Photography at the Lilly Library. His primary areas of research inv
 olve historic/antiquarian processes and the production of his own photogr
 aphic works using wet plate collodion\, gum bichromate\, anthotype\, and 
 cyanotype\, as well as camera obscuras and homemade pinhole cameras. Prio
 r to joining the Lilly Library team\, Scott was Professor of Art at Colum
 bia College (Columbia\, MO) where he taught darkroom and digital photogra
 phy and courses in the history of photography. Scott received his M.F.A. 
 in Photography from Massachusetts College of Art &amp\; Design in Boston\
 , MA. His work can be seen at scottmcmahonphoto.com (https://scottmcmahon
 photo.com/).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the Lilly Library's Curator of Pho
 tography for this behind-the-scenes look at photographs from their perman
 ent collection. As Indiana University's main library for rare books\, man
 uscripts\, and special collections participants will learn the role that 
 photography plays throughout the Lilly Library's collections. In addition
  to viewing a wonderful selection from throughout photographic history\, 
 we will get to hear about the upcoming exhibition <em>Harnessing Light: T
 racing Time Through Photography</em> opening at the Lilly Library early n
 ext year.</p><p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>Scott McMahon</strong>
  is Curator of Photography at the Lilly Library. His primary areas of res
 earch involve historic/antiquarian processes and the production of his ow
 n photographic works using wet plate collodion\, gum bichromate\, anthoty
 pe\, and cyanotype\, as well as camera obscuras and homemade pinhole came
 ras. <strong></strong>Prior to joining the Lilly Library team\, Scott was
  Professor of Art at Columbia College (Columbia\, MO) where he taught dar
 kroom and digital photography and courses in the history of photography. 
 Scott received his M.F.A. in Photography from Massachusetts College of Ar
 t &amp\; Design in Boston\, MA. His work can be seen at <a href="https://
 scottmcmahonphoto.com/">scottmcmahonphoto.com</a>.</p>
