DTSTART:20261204T150000Z
DTEND:20261204T210000Z
LOCATION:WYLIE HOUSE (307 E. SECOND STREET)
GEO:39.161697;-86.5309
SUMMARY:Winter Holiday Tours at Wylie House Museum
DESCRIPTION:The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh greenery and sea
 sonal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and holiday traditi
 ons to life.  Tours begin at the top of each hour\, with the final tour b
 eginning at 3 p.m.  No registration is needed\, but we ask that groups of
  8 or more contact us in advance at libwylie@iu.edu (mailto:libwylie@iu.e
 du) or (812) 855-6224.Parking: Designated\, free Wylie House parking spot
 s are located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via the
  alley. Free street parking is located directly in front of the museum on
  2nd St.Accessibility: The museum has accessible parking next to the muse
 um's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads to
  a ramp at the back door entrance of the museum. While the historic home'
 s second floor is only accessible by staircase\, digital images and virtu
 al tour options are provided for visitors who cannot visit the second flo
 or. Please contact us in advance of your visit to discuss any specific ne
 eds.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span class="TextRun SCXW253058102 BCX4" 
 lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTex
 tRun SCXW253058102 BCX4">The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh gre
 enery and seasonal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and ho
 liday traditions to life.</span></span></p><p>  Tours begin at the top of
  each hour\, with the final tour beginning at 3 p.m.</p><p>  No registrat
 ion is needed\, but we ask that groups of 8 or more contact us in advance
  at <a href="mailto:libwylie@iu.edu">libwylie@iu.edu</a> or (812) 855-622
 4.</p><p><strong>Parking:</strong> Designated\, free Wylie House parking 
 spots are located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via
  the alley. Free street parking is located directly in front of the museu
 m on 2nd St.</p><p><strong>Accessibility:</strong> The museum has accessi
 ble parking next to the museum's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center
 \, with a path that leads to a ramp at the back door entrance of the muse
 um. While the historic home's second floor is only accessible by staircas
 e\, digital images and virtual tour options are provided for visitors who
  cannot visit the second floor. Please contact us in advance of your visi
 t to discuss any specific needs.</p>
